<title>UK: Jacobs sells vessel for 6.25 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Jacobs sells vessel for 6.25 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK shippping, transport and property group Jacobs Holdings Plc said on Friday that it has sold a dry bulk carrier for 6.25 million stg to Tedross Navigation SA.</p>
<p>The vessel was acquired by Jacobs as part of its purchase of Ropner Plc.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it expects proceeds from the sale of the 1982-built Deerpool will be used to invest in roll-on, roll-off vessels.</p>
<p>Jacobs is also in negotiations to sell a second Ropner vessel.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
